I think the shopkeeper only keeps track of your actions while you are in the
shop, so that the shopkeeper ignores your pet, and also allows you to kick
things out of shops, if you are not standing in the shop.

I discovered something I thought was kind of neat.  I had a cloak of
invisibility, and the shopkeeper would not let me enter, so I took it off,
and he stood aside so I could enterm which I did.  Then I put it back on, 
and he blocked the entrance again, and would not move away from it.  Then I
found a wand of fire in the shop.  Hmmmm.  I zapped it at the shopkeeper,
but he lived.  3 more zaps, and the shopkeeper is still standing,
BUT HE HASN'T MOVED AWAY FROM THE DOOR!!!  Aha!  Target practice!  So he
stands there, and I let him have it from a distance with every knife, dagger,
dart, etc I have.  One time I stepped too close and he pounded me, but
I quickly stepped away, and he didn't follow.  So I root around the shop for
more stuff to throw, and eventually hit him enough to kill him and take his
gold, while remaining almost entirely unscathed myself.  The shop was then
mine for the taking.  Pretty neat.

